fontforge-wasm patch 4. Reason: CIDFlatten moves a CID-keyed font's lookups, kerning, names and features from the CID
master to the flattened font, but not its anchor classes; the master is then freed with them, so every anchor point
of the moved glyphs refers to freed memory, and writing the font (SFFindUnusedLookups) writes into it. Production's
FontForge 20190801 has the same omission. Found by the native ASan run (P2 plan, C1; owner's decision of 2026-11-18).

--- a/fontforge/fontforge/encoding.c
+++ b/fontforge/fontforge/encoding.c
@@ -1448,6 +1448,8 @@
 	bdf->sf = new;
     new->gpos_lookups = cidmaster->gpos_lookups;
     cidmaster->gpos_lookups = NULL;
+    new->anchor = cidmaster->anchor;	/* fontforge-wasm patch 4: the glyphs' anchor points refer to these */
+    cidmaster->anchor = NULL;
     new->gsub_lookups = cidmaster->gsub_lookups;
     cidmaster->gsub_lookups = NULL;
     new->kerns = cidmaster->kerns; new->vkerns = cidmaster->vkerns;
